msgid "**Handlers for Runtime Control:** Automatically builds, sets up, or restarts containers based on handlers. Notify ``compose up`` when rendered files or the service spec changed; notify ``container recreate`` when only in-container or in-database state changed and the process must reload it — the latter force-recreates in compose mode and forces a task recreation in swarm mode, where ``docker stack deploy`` alone would leave the running task untouched. To rebuild and recreate single services while the rest of the stack keeps running, set ``compose_service_up_targets`` to their service keys and notify ``compose-service-up``; it acts in compose mode only and recreates a service only when its image or configuration changed."
msgstr ""

