msgstr "**Hylättiin aikaisin:** tuntematon maku keskeyttää käytön luettelo kuljettaa makuja."

msgid "**Registration:** A throwaway instance registers its name together with a public key through ``utils.orchestrator.instance_api``; a later registration of the same name with a different key is refused, and the same key takes over, so a restarted instance keeps its name but a stranger cannot steal it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Registration:** A throwaway instance registers its name together with a public key through `utils.orchestrator.instance_api`; a later registration of the same name with a different key is refused, and the same key takes over, so a restarted instance keeps its name but a stranger cannot steal it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Registry and variant changes.** A variant can dictate the configuration of the providers it pulls in, and an MCP round decides for itself what it carries, which is the breaking change in this release. Fifteen moving pins gained names the registry can order, every MCP provider is registered as a shared service, *meta/schema.yml* finished its rename to *meta/secrets.yml*, role scripts are sorted into per-language folders, and *meta/addons* is now an accepted declaration site for pins and plugins."
msgstr "**Rekisterin ja muunnelman muutokset.** Muunnelma voi sanella palveluntarjoajien kokoonpanon se vetää sisään, ja MCP kierros päättää itse, mitä se kuljettaa, joka on rikkoa muutos tässä julkaisussa. Viisitoista liikkuvaa nastaa sai nimiä rekisterin voi tilata, jokainen MCP palveluntarjoaja on rekisteröity yhteisen palvelun, *meta/schema.yml* päätti nimensä *meta/secrets.yml*, rooli skriptit on lajiteltu per-kieli kansiot, ja *meta/addonit* on nyt hyväksytty ilmoitus sivusto nastat ja plugins."

msgid "**Registry proxy.** When the stack's docker daemon pulls through a registry proxy (the local registry cache), the runner's nested daemon uses the same proxy via a `docker.service` drop-in and, when the outer daemon trusts the cache's CA, fetches that CA from the proxy before it starts."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Registry proxy.** When the stack’s docker daemon pulls through a registry proxy (the local registry cache), the runner’s nested daemon uses the same proxy via a ``docker.service`` drop-in and, when the outer daemon trusts the cache’s CA, fetches that CA from the proxy before it starts."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Registry report:** ``make security-runtimes`` lists the PHP runtime of every pinned image from registry metadata, without pulling, against the same floors."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Registry report:** `make security-runtimes` lists the PHP runtime of every pinned image from registry metadata, without pulling, against the same floors."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Release pushes on main.** A push to *main* whose head commit starts with *Release version* cancels the running *main* pipeline, so the release starts at once. A release-tagged commit deploys every chunk instead of stopping at the first failed one, and still ends red when any chunk fails, which keeps a broken release from being published. A new integration test requires every release tag from v13.0.0 on to sit on that subject, and the test job now checks out the full history with tags."
msgstr ""

