msgid "**Role Groups:** `files/sql/reconcile-roles.sql <./files/sql/reconcile-roles.sql>`__ creates the accounts of the ``administrator`` and ``collaborator`` role group members that have none yet and sets the role of every account to administrator, collaborator or visitor from its groups. It runs through ``psql`` in the database container as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer, so a group change reaches Fider within one timer interval. The platform administrator keeps its role."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role Mapping At Sign-In:** The role-local plugin [files/php/infinito_rbac_login.php](./files/php/infinito_rbac_login.php) applies the same rules to the account that signs in through RebelOIDC, read from the `groups` claim of the ID token of that sign-in, so a role-group change and a website added later reach the account at its next sign-in instead of the next timer run. A sign-in without a `groups` claim changes nothing, a password login is never touched, and neither are the local superuser and the anonymous account. The deploy installs and activates the plugin together with RebelOIDC and writes its group paths to the `[InfinitoRbacLogin]` section of `config/config.ini.php`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role Mapping At Sign-In:** The role-local plugin `files/php/infinito_rbac_login.php <./files/php/infinito_rbac_login.php>`__ applies the same rules to the account that signs in through RebelOIDC, read from the ``groups`` claim of the ID token of that sign-in, so a role-group change and a website added later reach the account at its next sign-in instead of the next timer run. A sign-in without a ``groups`` claim changes nothing, a password login is never touched, and neither are the local superuser and the anonymous account. The deploy installs and activates the plugin together with RebelOIDC and writes its group paths to the ``[InfinitoRbacLogin]`` section of ``config/config.ini.php``."
