msgid "Before act starts, `make swarm-zombie` runs a disk pre-flight ([`swarm_preflight.py`](../../../../cli/meta/ci/swarm_preflight.py)): it prints the include set the provision step derives for the round, pruned by `disable=` as the provision step prunes it, with the `min_storage` each role declares, and refuses when that total plus the watchdog floor exceeds the lowest free space of Docker's data root and the roots the watchdog samples, so a round that never fit fails in seconds instead of at the watchdog an hour in. The total is a heuristic: it leaves out the roles `extend_inventory` adds per host and a disable list of the CI matrix row, and `min_storage` mixes image bytes with data reservations. `preflight=false` skips it. A host-mode-only role such as `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` has no swarm row of its own; it rides on a host row, and [`host_rows.py`](../../../../cli/meta/ci/host_rows.py) ranks the rows whose include set carries it by that same declared storage, lightest first (`python -m cli.meta.ci.host_rows --provides container_backup --mode swarm`). A light host does not carry every subject kind the role's own restore cycle handles, such as the Discourse launcher container, so keep one heavy host for the final or CI round."
msgstr ""

