msgid "Behind the front proxy every object icon the app loads by URL is a broken image, among them the header logo as soon as the object icon `agent-portal-logo` exists. The frontend serves such an icon at `/objecticons/<id>/image%2Fpng` (route `/objecticons/:iconId/:contentType`), and the request reaches it with the encoded slash decoded, so the route does not match and the application document answers. Measured from inside the stack without a session: `http://127.0.0.1:8083/objecticons/1/image%2Fpng` (the role's own proxy) answers 200, `http://127.0.0.1:8083/objecticons/1/image/png` answers 302 and `https://kix.infinito.test/objecticons/1/image%2Fpng` answers 302; signed in, the header logo URL answered 200 with `text/html` and 86854 bytes. Cause: the front proxy vhost normalises the request path, shared code outside this role. Until that is fixed the role stylesheet carries the header logo from the CDN (`#kix-header #logo` in `files/style.css`). Options: hand the request URI to this app unchanged in the front proxy and then drop that stylesheet rule; or keep the rule."
