msgid "Drop the `php_memory_unlimited` mount ([memory-unlimited.ini](roles/sys-svc-compose-php/files/memory-unlimited.ini), `memory_limit = -1`) from each role whose image ships PHP 8.2.35, 8.3.36, 8.4.27, 8.5.12 or later, and the file, its install task, `FILE_PHP_MEMORY_UNLIMITED_INI` and [its lint](tests/lint/ansible/roles/meta/test_php_memory_unlimited_reaches_fpm.py) once no role mounts it. It is the interim mitigation for CVE-2026-109618 and overrides the per-role `service_memory_mb` share, so a single request can exhaust the container instead of hitting a PHP limit. Still mounted by `web-app-magento` (`markoshust/magento-php:8.4-fpm`, PHP 8.4.21) and `web-app-mailu` (`ghcr.io/mailu/webmail:2024.06`, which every flavor runs). `web-app-fusiondirectory` (`nfrastack/fusiondirectory:1.5`, PHP 7.4.33 on Alpine 3.15, end of life and never patched) carries it as `PHP_MEMORY_LIMIT=-1` in `templates/env.j2` instead (the image's pool sets `php_admin_value[memory_limit]` from it, so a conf.d ini cannot reach FPM) and drops it under the same rule. `web-app-magento` keeps the 756M its `nginx.conf.sample` (`PHP_VALUE`) and `pub/.user.ini` set and keeps `post_max_size` below a quarter of that limit."
