msgid "Every deploy converges `verifyEmail` onto an existing realm, and the federation sets `trustEmail: true`, which Keycloak 26.8.2 applies only when it first imports a user (`LDAPStorageProvider.doImportUser`); the deploy stamps the users imported earlier before the converge. A local realm user that a deploy creates after the converge (`06_users/realm.yml`) is unverified until the inventory stamp at the end of the same deploy, so a login in that window gets the link. An address that changes in LDAP outside Keycloak keeps the user's `emailVerified` flag, because the LDAP sync writes `email` without touching it. A user of an `external` realm with SMTP who holds no address yet can still set one in `UPDATE_PROFILE` or `VERIFY_PROFILE`: Keycloak 26.8.1 lets that profile form write a blank `email`, and the user profile config cannot make it admin-only for that case, because its `edit` permission knows only the roles `admin` and `user`. Keycloak then adds `UPDATE_EMAIL`, so the login only finishes once the user follows the confirmation link. Until then the address already sits in Keycloak and, through the writable federation, in LDAP `mail`. A Keycloak event listener or a profile validator that refuses a first address outside `UPDATE_EMAIL` would close that gap."
