msgid "Judge each piece on its own: a backdrop blend is not a forgotten grey, a data colour is not a brand colour. Look, screenshot by screenshot."
msgstr ""

msgid "Judge it by the log instead, and start with the check that works for **every** target: `grep -aE 'make: \\*\\*\\*|Error [0-9]+' /tmp/<name>.log`. Then assert the artefact the run was supposed to produce (the file it writes, the count it changes). Only aggregate targets additionally offer the `📊 per-target wall-clock` table and the `FAILED TARGETS:` line, because `scripts/make/parallel.sh` emits those; a single-recipe target such as `i18n-extract` prints neither, so looking for the table there finds nothing and tempts you back to the exit code."
msgstr ""

msgid "Judge the gate by its table, never by the exit code."
msgstr ""

msgid "Judging the engine alone made ``make test-oracle`` vacuous: ``make i18n`` deploys the engine on its own, so a lane whose engine served counted as up while System One was down, and the oracle suite skipped itself to a green exit. Every role the caller names is probed, which is why the runner republishes System One's port too."
