msgid "Python compares the parsed tree plus a leading ``#`` line (a shebang or a coding cookie), so comments, blank lines, quotes and line wraps drop out while a changed docstring or interpreter still counts. YAML and JSON compare the loaded data with mapping order kept and every scalar tagged with its type: a template that iterates a mapping renders its keys in file order, and ``1``, ``1.0`` and ``true`` load equal in Python but render differently. YAML and JSON under a role's ``files/`` or ``templates/`` ship to a program whose parser may read ``on``, ``1.10`` or a duplicate key otherwise, so only an identical text is format-only there. The same holds for a text carrying a comment a deploy or a deployed program reads (:data:`READ_COMMENTS`): dropping comments would hide an edit of it. Those comments are a Python coding cookie and the ``WANT_JSON`` marker Ansible reads in a module, the ``# variant-pin:`` of :mod:`utils.roles.applications.variant_pins` and the ``# nocheck:`` rules whose reader is not a lint: ``inventory-open-subtree`` (:mod:`cli.administration.inventory.validate.open_subtrees`) and ``inventory-variable`` (:mod:`cli.administration.inventory.validate.variables`), which the inventory validator of every dedicated deploy reads, and ``header-trust`` (:mod:`utils.roles.header_trust`) and ``license-declared`` (:mod:`utils.licensing.roles`), which the docs build of ``web-app-docs`` renders. Every other file kind, an added or deleted file and a side that does not parse count as a real change, which keeps the classifier from cutting what it cannot read."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Python packaging and dependency-reference rules: `pyproject.toml` requirement coverage, ban on stale `requirements/NNN-…` numbers in code, the deprecated-`pkgmgr` warning, and Galaxy/git parity of the Ansible collection requirements (suppression rule key `galaxy-git-parity`)."
msgstr "Python-pakkaukset ja riippuvuuden viitesäännöt: `pyproject.toml` vaatimuskattavuus, vanhentunut kielto `requirements/NNN-…` koodinumerot, poistot...`pkgmgr` Varoitus, ja Galaxy / git pariteetti Ansible keräysvaatimukset (Purkamissäännön avain `galaxy-git-parity`)."

