msgid "The group map covers the `administrator` (Super Users, id 8), `manager` (Manager, id 6), `publisher` (Publisher, id 5), `editor` (Editor, id 4), `author` (Author, id 3) and `registered` (Registered, id 2) roles. A user whose groups claim matches none of them lands in the com_users \"New User Registration Group\" (`new_usertype`, `Registered` by default). The Joomla account is created on first login if it does not already exist. Every login re-syncs the group memberships, name, email, frontend language and time zone from Keycloak. The `locale` claim maps to the installed site language with the same tag, then to the first installed language with the same primary subtag (`de` resolves to `de-DE`), else to the site default. The `zoneinfo` claim maps to the time zone when PHP knows it, else to the site default. The plugin requests the `phone` and `address` scopes and writes the mapped claims into the `profile` data that the core `plg_user_profile` stores; a claim the ID token does not carry clears its field. Every login stores the name through the `string` input filter and the email in its punycode form, the values the com_users profile save produces, marks the account with the `keycloak_managed` user parameter, forks the session and marks it with `keycloak.sso_session`. A local sign-in clears that mark (`onUserAfterLogin`); for a marked account other than the bootstrap administrator (`JOOMLA_ADMIN_USERNAME`) it signs the account out again and sends it to `task=login`, so a marked account holds a site session through Keycloak only. The com_users profile form of a marked account renders the fields `JOOMLA_OIDC_PROFILE_LOCKED` names read-only and marks each with `data-infinito-sso-locked` (`onContentPrepareForm`, after every other plugin), and a profile save keeps their stored values (`onContentNormaliseRequestData`); a local session of the bootstrap administrator or of an account holding `core.admin` is break-glass and edits its own profile freely. `onUserBeforeSave` throws when a site request outside the break-glass session or a web services API request changes a locked field or `keycloak_managed` of a marked account; the callback's own provisioning write, the console and the backend pass. A field whose key `JOOMLA_OIDC_PROFILE_LOCKED` does not list stays editable; the next login still overwrites it. The backend is break-glass only: the callback runs on the site client, so a backend session never carries `keycloak.sso_session` and its user form is not locked. The role's `services.sso.profile.locked` selectors match the marker, so the shared lock renderer adds the warning only to fields the plugin locked. A valid com_users `user.logout` request of a signed-in site user takes the `task=logout` path below."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The group stays primary. It reaps within seconds of a run being created and needs no runner, while the fallback first has to win a runner slot — from the very pool the superseded sweep is saturating, so it is slowest exactly when it is needed. Measured waits in this repository range from under a minute to about twenty. That is the cost of the fallback, and the reason it is a fallback rather than the mechanism."
msgstr "Ryhmä pysyy ensisijaisena. Se niittää sekunneissa juoksu on luotu ja tarvitsee ei juoksijaa, kun taas varalla ensin on voittaa juoksija paikka ... aivan uima-altaasta korvattu pyyhkäisy on kyllästävä, joten se on hitain juuri kun sitä tarvitaan. Mitatut odotukset tässä arkistossa vaihtelevat alle minuutista noin kahteenkymmeneen. Se on varauksen hinta, ja se on pikemminkin varatoimenpide kuin mekanismi."

