msgid "The total is a heuristic, not a measurement. The include set leaves out the roles extend_inventory adds per host (svc-swarm-node, the NFS server, WireGuard, the backup host) and does not see a disable list the CI matrix row adds on its own. The declared sum is also deliberately not multiplied by the swarm node count: min_storage mixes image bytes, which every node that runs a task pulls, with data reservations, which land once on the NFS export or never fill, so no single factor fits every role, and a per-node factor would refuse every row that carries a large reservation such as the mail server's. A measured web-app-wordpress#0 run consumed more than its deployed roles declared, which is why the in-run watchdog stays the guard beyond this check."
