msgid "When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT’s native ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` is enabled via the ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = INFINITO_SSO_USER``). nginx gates ``/login`` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak, injects the verified ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header and sends the ``sso_proxy_secret`` credential as ``X-Infinito-Sso-Proxy`` with every request. Apache in the container copies the username into the ``INFINITO_SSO_USER`` server variable only when that secret matches ``INFINITO_SSO_PROXY_SECRET``. Snipe-IT matches the username against ``users.username`` (the user must pre-exist and be activated, see the RBAC feature below) to mint a native ``snipeit_session``. Visitors without a matching activated user fall through to the normal login form, where a directory sign-in creates the account. The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr ""

