msgid "[x] A dedicated Semaphore runner container runs every template; its image is the Infinito.Nexus image with the tag of the current deploy, never `latest`; it mounts no Docker socket, runs as a non-root user, and reaches hosts only over SSH with a key held in the Semaphore key store. The server sets `SEMAPHORE_USE_REMOTE_RUNNER=true` unconditionally ([env.j2](../../roles/web-app-semaphore/templates/env.j2) line 17), the `task-runner` service mounts only its runner-token secret ([meta/volumes.yml](../../roles/web-app-semaphore/meta/volumes.yml) lines 8-16) and runs as UID and GID 64101 through the last `USER` of its [Dockerfile](../../roles/web-app-semaphore/files/runner/Dockerfile) (line 36), and its env carries no key, so the app-control and deploy keys reach it only from the key store of the project (`ensure_ssh_key` in [project.py](../../roles/web-app-semaphore/files/python/project.py) line 153). [test_runner_isolation.py](../../tests/unit/python/roles/web-app-semaphore/test_runner_isolation.py) holds all four, with a local runner, a conditional remote runner, a socket mount, a literal socket volume, a root `USER`, a root UID and a key in the runner env as negative controls. `test_the_own_round_builds_on_the_image_of_this_deploy` and `test_an_empty_deploy_base_fails` in [test_runner_build.py](../../tests/unit/python/roles/web-app-semaphore/test_runner_build.py) pin the base image to `SOFTWARE_IMAGE:SOFTWARE_IMAGE_TAG` (`ci-<sha>` in CI, `dev-<sha>` locally, `v<version>` in production; a deploy that pulls Semaphore in only as a provider keeps the runner it deployed, per [073](073-semaphore-runner-build-on-input-change.md)), and `test_the_inventory_carries_the_app_control_key` in [test_project.py](../../tests/unit/python/roles/web-app-semaphore/files/test_project.py) binds the SSH key to the inventory the templates run on."
msgstr ""

