msgid "`start.yml <tasks/utils/prepull/start.yml>`__ pulls the images the deploy of the host runs, as listed by the ``update_pull_images`` filter, that the host does not hold yet under the pinned reference (`pull.yml <tasks/utils/prepull/pull.yml>`__), three at a time in a background job right before the shared services load; with nothing missing no job starts. It runs when ``STORAGE_CONSTRAINED`` and ``RESET`` are false and the host is a stack host, so never on a swarm worker. `reap.yml <tasks/utils/prepull/reap.yml>`__ collects the job before the E2E run, or at the start of the destructor on a host without a server stage, and prints the pulls that failed. A failed pull or the time limit of ``SYS_SVC_CONTAINER_PREPULL_ASYNC_TIME`` does not fail the deploy, and each app still pulls its images itself."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`start_interval` is the cadence while `start_period` is still running. Without it a probe only fires every `interval`, so a service ready after three seconds is reported healthy at the next tick -- 30s, or a minute for the curl flavors -- and a stack converges no faster than its slowest quantisation. It changes when the same probe runs, never what it tests."
msgstr "`start_interval` on poljin `start_period` Se on yhä käynnissä. Ilman sitä luotain ampuu vain jokaisen `interval`, Palvelu on valmis kolmen sekunnin kuluttua. 30s, tai minuutti kihara maku -- ja pino lähenee ei nopeammin kuin sen hitain kvantitalisaatio. Se muuttuu, kun sama luotain toimii."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`start_period` therefore bounds it: once the window closes the cadence falls back to `interval`, so a service that becomes ready just after the window pays a full tick anyway. The window has to outlast a realistic boot, not merely a fast one, which is why it is measured in minutes rather than sized to `interval`. It costs nothing while the container works, only the time until a broken one is called unhealthy."
msgstr "`start_period` siis sitoo sen: kun ikkuna sulkeutuu, polku laskee takaisin `interval`, joten palvelu, joka tulee valmiiksi heti ikkunan maksaa koko punkin joka tapauksessa. Ikkunan on kestettävä realistinen saapas, ei vain nopea, minkä vuoksi se mitataan minuutteina eikä kooltaan `interval`. Se ei maksa mitään, kun kontti toimii, vain aikaa, kunnes rikki yksi kutsutaan epäterve."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`stdio_only`, not `hosted_only`. The audit of `discourse/discourse-mcp` at `v0.3.1` closed the sidecar path: ownership, licence, pinning and read-only default pass, but the HTTP transport serves one session per process. Nothing is enabled until upstream supports concurrent sessions."
msgstr "`stdio_only`, ei `hosted_only`. `discourse/discourse-mcp` klo `v0.3.1` sulje sivuvaunupolku: omistus, lisenssi, pinning ja luku-only oletuspassi, mutta HTTP kuljetus palvelee yksi istunto per prosessi. Mikään ei ole käytössä ennen kuin ylävirta tukee samanaikaisia istuntoja."

msgid "`storages` is provisioned entirely from the other side: [web-app-nextcloud](../web-app-nextcloud/) container-execs into this role's web container and creates the `Storages::NextcloudStorage`, its OAuth application and the matching Nextcloud client. The deploy order places this role before `web-app-nextcloud`, so nothing of that exists while this role runs and its hook stays empty."
